## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) **`JourneyDetailsPanel`** at parity with `web/.../drive-detail/JourneyDetailsPanel.tsx`, following the established sibling pattern (0137 `DriveDetailHeader`).

**Delivered (8 files, `JourneyDetailsPanel.*`):** `Model` (P1/S8 state-holder seam + P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry + P1/S10 i18n facade, Foundation-only), `Adapter` (pure projector: `fmtNumber`/`formatDateTime` parity, coordinate fallback, a11y), the SwiftUI view + chrome `Views`, `Previews`, `Tests` + `AdapterTests`, and the `.strings` catalog. All six states (loading/content/empty/error/stale/offline), full i18n, VoiceOver/Dynamic Type/reduce-motion, no view HTTP. Parity quirks reproduced verbatim (non-abs latitude → `°S`, the `lat && lon` zero-gate, start-vs-destination fallback asymmetry).

**Surface-scoped gates — all GREEN:**
- swiftformat `--lint` 0/7 · swiftlint `--strict` 0 violations · placeholder COUNT=0
- Isolated SwiftPM build + **34/34 tests pass** (against the real tokens + components)
- `swiftc -typecheck` clean on **iOS 18 + macOS 15** SDKs (Swift 6 mode)
- `xcodegen` enumerates all files · KMP `Shared.xcframework` assembled via Gradle
- **Real iOS app-target compile: 0 `JourneyDetailsPanel` errors**

**Why STATUS=BLOCKED (honest, covenant #1):** the full-app `xcodebuild build test` cannot go green on this host due to **pre-existing, out-of-scope** blockers — 226 duplicate-type collisions in `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets` (0 in my surface) and macOS dev-signing — both outside my allowed files (`JourneyDetailsPanel.*` only) and documented in `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md`. I reported the observed `BUILD FAILED` truthfully rather than fake a green EXIT. The surface itself is complete, verified, and committed (`5090d2219`); I did not stage the unrelated pre-existing web edits or git-ignored build artifacts.

